= The Open Letter

In December the Stuttgart metalworkers, led by communists, won the local SPD and USPD branches and the unions to a common list of demands. [? if levi_in_party = 1 : Levi and Radek ?][? if levi_in_party = 0 : Radek and the union men of the Right ?] want to make the same offer to the whole country.

The draft is ready for the Rote Fahne of 8 January. It proposes joint action for wages and pensions, workers' control of food supplies, the disarming of the civil guards and trade with Soviet Russia. It does not ask anyone to accept the dictatorship of the proletariat first. Ruth Fischer calls it an invitation to the men of 1919 to take our workers back.

- @sincere: Publish the letter, and mean it.
- @manoeuvre: Publish it so that the workers see who refuses.
- @shelve: Put it back in the drawer.

@sincere
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Social democratic workers will remember it the next time we ask them for something. Radek will be pleased, Zinoviev less so.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any offer to the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.open_letter = 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.ecci('radek', 8);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -5);
RG.ledger('The Open Letter of January 1921 offered the whole labour movement joint action.', 'e21_open_letter');
!}

The letter appears on 8 January. The *Vorwärts* calls it a manoeuvre and the union leaders refuse it within the week. But it is read out at factory meetings across Germany, and at many of them the social democratic workers vote for it.

@manoeuvre
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Both wings of the party can live with it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any offer to the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.open_letter = 2;
Q.unity += 4;
Q.spd_relation -= 3;
!}

The letter is published with a commentary predicting its rejection, and the prediction comes true. The *Vorwärts* quotes the commentary back at us.

@shelve
subtitle: The Left will like this. The Stuttgart comrades will not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.open_letter = 0;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 8;
RG.district('berlin', {loyalty: 5});
!}

The draft goes back in the drawer. In Stuttgart the comrades who started it all are told to dissolve their joint committee. Some of them do.
